1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,430
Rain hammers down on Interlagos — race day in São Paulo, round twenty of the 2026 season.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,530
Antonelli arrived already a champion — the youngest in history, crowned in Mexico City one week ago. Today, São Paulo decides the constructors' title.

3
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:29,030
Norris has pole. Beside him, the champion — Antonelli on the front row. Slot twenty-one: Verstappen, after a thirty-place power-unit penalty.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,140
Seventy-one laps. Lights out — and into Turn One, the champion goes around the pole-sitter! Antonelli leads the Grand Prix!

5
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:50,930
Nineteen laps the champion leads. Then lap twenty — the Senna S. Antonelli skates across the gravel; Norris sweeps into the lead!

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,800
From dead last, Max Verstappen starts to carve.

7
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,300
Overtake after overtake — twenty-first to second!

8
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:21,360
Norris holds on from pole! Hadjar completes a Red Bull double. Russell fourth — the champion fifth… and Mercedes?

9
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:36,810
Constructors' champions. Norris by fourteen-point-six. Hadjar completes a Red Bull double — third. Russell fourth. The champion fifth, fastest lap of the race. Piastri sixth.

10
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:48,100
One week, two championships. Mexico City gave Mercedes the drivers'. São Paulo hands them the constructors'. Double champions — 2026!
